af28c01ce9f96","event_uuid":"8bf5bc80-7abe-4b24-9af7-5287510bb8dc","position":{"commit_sha":"e645cf10aaa1c390139f6822a3279f1c2f555ec5","position":"1788445933906393001-8bf5bc80-7abe-4b24-9af7-5287510bb8dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788444111173484001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` already owns the extracted `_llm_*` reader helpers from ticket 02b7. The remaining janitor target is the still-inline composition block inside `LLMConfig.from_env`: after tombstone checks, table/CLI loading, and runtime-path resolution, `from_env` still spells out a long sequence of per-field `_llm_str` / `_llm_int` / `_llm_float` calls and overlap assignments before the final `cls(...)`.\n\n## Approach\n\nKeep `LLMConfig.from_env` as the sole precedence/composition facade and keep the target basename `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py` unchanged. Extract cohesive helper assemblers in that existing leaf for the current field groups so `from_env` shrinks to orchestration: load table/CLI state, resolve runtime-only roots and tombstones, call the grouped assemblers, and construct `cls(...)`. Do not introduce new sibling module names; existing guards and AST tests already pin `config_readers.py` as the composition-root leaf.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py`\n- `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_config_llm.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py`\n\n## Testing\n\nRun focused config precedence/default/error tests that cover config-file, environment, explicit override, malformed value, missing value, cross-field precedence, and the monkeypatch-visible import surface, plus lint/typecheck/module-size/complexity gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Cohesive helper assemblers for the existing field groups move the repetitive per-field resolution out of `LLMConfig.from_env` while reusing the current `_llm_*` readers in `config_readers.py`.\n- [ ] `LLMConfig.from_env` remains the only place that performs tombstone enforcement, loads the merged config table/CLI overrides, resolves runtime-only repo/tickets roots, and constructs `LLMConfig`.\n- [ ] The `config_readers.py` basename and monkeypatch-visible behavior stay unchanged, and defaults, validation failures, and precedence remain value-equivalent.\n- [ ] Focused config tests plus lint, typecheck, module-size, and complexity gates pass.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"reduce the facade to tombstone/runtime-root orchestration plus grouped reader assembly"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py","reason":"own the extracted grouped scalar readers for model/provider, limits, and overlap settings"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_llm.py","reason":"prove from_env delegates grouped scalar resolution through monkeypatch-visible helpers without changing precedence"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py","reason":"preserve pointed-file precedence and layering behavior across the extraction"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py","reason":"preserve gate-root config discovery after moving grouped readers"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerate the environment registry after the LLM config env readers move into config_readers.py"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","86c0-59ec-a28b-4f7c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"86c0-59ec-a28b-4f7c","pa